  "schemaGuide": "A field line reads `name: type = default [flags]`; R required, W writable, B bindable, C construction-only.",
  "schemas": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "A material with a fragment stage",
      "source": "// A material's `fragment` runs per pixel on the GPU; the `fn` helpers it calls must be GPU-safe.\nfn pulse(t: f32) -> f32 {\n    return 0.65 + 0.35 * sin(t);\n}\n\nmaterial Pulse {\n    param tint: color = #6b5cff;\n    param phase: f32 = 0.0;\n\n    fragment(input: SurfaceInput) -> color {\n        return color.linear(tint.rgb * pulse(phase), tint.a);\n    }\n}\n\nscene Demo {\n    camera Main {\n        position: vec3(0.0, 2.0, 5.0);\n        target: vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n    }\n\n    entity Cube {\n        mesh: Box {};\n        material: Pulse { phase: bind(frame.time); };\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bind a material parameter to scene state",
      "source": "// A material declares params with defaults; `bind(name)` keeps a param equal to scene state.\nmaterial Tinted {\n    param tint: color = #6b5cff;\n\n    fragment(input: SurfaceInput) -> color {\n        return tint;\n    }\n}\n\nscene Demo {\n    state tint: color = #ff8a3d;\n\n    camera Main {\n        position: vec3(0.0, 2.0, 5.0);\n        target: vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n    }\n\n    entity Cube {\n        mesh: Box {};\n        material: Tinted { tint: bind(tint); };\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Prefabs and prefab instances",
      "source": "// A prefab is a reusable entity with params; `entity Name: Prefab { param: value; }` makes one.\nprefab Crate {\n    param origin: vec3 = vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n    param tint: color = #5b8def;\n\n    position: origin;\n    mesh: Box {};\n    material: Pbr { base_color: tint; };\n}\n\nscene Demo {\n    camera Main {\n        position: vec3(0.0, 3.0, 8.0);\n        target: vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n    }\n\n    entity Left: Crate {\n        origin: vec3(-1.5, 0.5, 0.0);\n    }\n\n    entity Right: Crate {\n        origin: vec3(1.5, 0.5, 0.0);\n        tint: #ff8a3d;\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Animate an entity in update",
      "source": "// `update(dt)` runs every frame; assign to `self.rotation` to turn the entity.\nscene Demo {\n    state speed: f32 = 0.7;\n\n    camera Main {\n        position: vec3(0.0, 2.0, 5.0);\n        target: vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n    }\n\n    entity Cube {\n        mesh: Box {};\n        position: vec3(0.0, 0.5, 0.0);\n\n        update(dt: f32) {\n            self.rotation *= quat.axis_angle(vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), speed * dt);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"
    }
  ],
  "diagnosticsGuide": "`mtek check --format json` prints one JSON report; each diagnostic has code, severity, title, message, source (file, startByte, endByte, startLine, startColumn, endLine, endColumn), expected and actual (when relevant), related, notes, suggestedEdits and phase. Fix errors in report order, apply a suggestedEdit only when it is present (they are validated), and never delete the feature a diagnostic is about."
